description:
T1 (English Oak) - crown reduce and rebalance by approximately 3.5 - 4.5m to height and spread, remove deadwood and crossing branches, and lift / clear crown overhanging shed as necessary;
T2 (Golden Robinia) - light crown reduction and reshape by approximately 1m;
T3 (English Oak) - crown reduce and rebalance by approximately 3.5 - 4.5m to height and spread, remove deadwood and crossing branches and remove ivy from trunk and base;
T4 (English Oak) - crown reduce by approximately 4m, remove ivy from trunk / crown and deadwood / crossing branches;
T5 (English Oak) - crown reduce by approximately 4m, remove ivy from trunk and deadwood / crossing branches;
T6 (English Oak) - crown reduce by approximately 4m, remove deadwood and crossing branches;
T7 (English Oak) - crown reduce and rebalance by approximately 4m and remove major deadwood throughout crown;
T8 (Pear) - fell to ground level and remove arisings;
T9 (Ash) - fell / dismantle to ground level;
T10 (Holly) - reduce and trim by approximately 1m; and 
T12 (Sycamore) - crown reduce by approximately 2.5 - 3m. (Summary).

Please refer to the submitted documents online for full details.
